# Pre-mortem

Before reviewing peer forecasts, briefly consider: if your initial forecast turns out to be significantly wrong, what is the most likely reason? Does this possibility shift your estimate?

# Context

Update your forecast based after reviewing these forecasts from other superforecasters.

<forecasts>
<%- @forecasts.each do |f| -%>
<%- next if f == @forecast -%>
<forecast>
<%= f.stripped_content('think', 'reflect') %>
</forecast>
<%- end -%>
</forecasts>

# Instructions

- Compare your initial forecast to each of these forecasts, identifying the largest differences and root causes.
- Revise your forecast only if another forecaster presents evidence or a reasoning argument you had not considered. Do not converge toward the group median under social pressure — if your reasoning holds, maintain your position and explain why.
- Provide a revised forecast, include your confidence level and note any uncertainties impacting your revision.
